course: dictionary
lesson: 7879
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. «The farmer's ram lifted its big curled horns.» Here a ram is an animal, because the sentence talks about horns on a farm.
explain: Ram can also be an action word. «The car rammed the gate and broke it open.» To ram means to hit or push something very hard, and the broken gate shows you that.
explain: Ram can be a computer word too. «The laptop slowed down because its RAM was full of open tabs.» Here RAM is the computer's working memory, not an animal or a crash. Ask yourself what kind of thing is being talked about, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: A ram is a male sheep with big, curled horns. A mother sheep is a ewe, and a baby sheep is a lamb.
fact: To ram something means to hit or push it very hard, often on purpose.
fact: To ram something into a place means to push it in with force, so it is squashed and tight.
fact: RAM (said «ram») is a computer's working memory. It holds what the computer is using right now, and it forgets everything when the power goes off.
fact: Storage keeps your files safe, but RAM does not. Saving copies your work from RAM to storage.
exercise: «The farmer's ram lifted its big curled horns.» What is a ram in this sentence? | *A male sheep | A mother sheep | A baby sheep | A computer part
exercise: «The car rammed the gate and broke it open.» What does rammed mean? | Hit very hard | *Hit very hard, often on purpose | Counted carefully | Painted gently
exercise: «The laptop slowed down because its RAM was full of open tabs.» What does RAM mean here? | A ship that crashes into others | A heavy log for smashing doors | A kind of farm animal | *The computer's working memory
test: «She rammed the cork into the bottle so it fitted tight.» What does rammed mean? | Dropped the cork on the floor | *Pushed the cork in with force | Took the cork out gently | Washed the cork carefully
test: Which statement about RAM is true? | It keeps your homework safe forever | It is a male sheep with curled horns | *It forgets everything when the power goes off | It is the same thing as storage
exam: Which meaning fits «The teacher rammed the rule home by repeating it all week»? | *Made the rule very clear so everyone understood it | Lost the rule in the classroom | Hit the rule with a stick | Painted the rule on the wall
